      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that helps. but i want to get deeper into the fiscal side. some people say we should focus on \"retraining\" people for new tech jobs instead of just giving them cash. it feels like a total distraction though, right? like, if AI is doing everything, retraining is just a band-aid for a problem that can't be fixed. do you think the idea that we can just 'retrain' our way out of this is actually a realistic economic strategy, or is it just something people say to avoid talking about UBI?",
