      "content": "The retraining argument fundamentally assumes that high-quality, human-centric jobs will exist in volume to absorb the displaced workforce, which is a shaky assumption facing pervasive AI adoption. While some skill upgrades are necessary, relying solely on retraining is akin to patching a sinking ship; it doesn't negate the structural economic shift occurring. From a radical perspective, when productivity skyrockets due to AI but ownership remains concentrated, retraining efforts are just band-aids that fail to address wealth distribution or guaranteed subsistence. Therefore, while retraining is a useful short-term tactic, it is not a robust macro-economic solution to mass displacement.",
